From 794172be404e4c8ec64572ba9aae7421f12225c5
Subject: bevy_asset: use futures-channel mpsc for the wasm threaded loader
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/794172be404e4c8ec64572ba9aae7421f12225c5
Date: 2026-06-18T18:00:16+01:00

On `wasm32` with atomics, `async-channel`'s send/notify and receiver
registration take a blocking lock (`event_listener`'s `std::Mutex`). When
contended, that lock lowers to `memory.atomic.wait`, which is only legal on a
worker — on the main (window) thread it traps. The `AssetServer` drives loads
from the main thread, so the trap intermittently aborts an in-flight load
mid-poll, leaving the asset stuck (it never completes and never errors).

Switch the wasm threaded loader's request and reply channels to
`futures::channel::mpsc::unbounded`, whose `unbounded_send`/notify path is
lock-free (a brief spinlock, not a futex), so the main thread never reaches
`memory.atomic.wait`. `futures-channel` is already in the dependency tree via
`bevy_tasks`, so this adds no new dependency.
